WEBVTT


00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.160
Personal brand teaching traveling around the world

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.880
I always say the same thing to people.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.960
It's not who you know,

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.600
is the one who knows you.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.640
Today I can open up many opportunities,

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:10.760
not only because of the personal brand I have,

00:00:10.761 --> 00:00:12.401
but sometimes I don't have the contact with the person.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:13.560
That person has seen me,

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:14.640
has seen my personal brand,

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.160
someone has told him about her.

00:00:16.161 --> 00:00:18.041
And when we talk about it being a personal brand,

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:19.360
the most basic definition

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:21.560
personal mark is how you present yourself,

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.040
but also how they perceive you.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.360
Many people work hard in biography.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:26.284
perfect. 

00:00:26.284 --> 00:00:27.360
I am number one,

00:00:27.361 --> 00:00:28.361
I am the leader

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.120
and that can often even be left in front or not.

00:00:31.121 --> 00:00:32.481
There is evidence to support this.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:33.252
However, 

00:00:33.252 --> 00:00:34.080
the perception

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.560
is what they say about you when you are not in the room.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.600
How do people describe you too?

00:00:38.601 --> 00:00:39.321
So I, for example,

00:00:39.322 --> 00:00:40.801
when I ask people how

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.480
describe Vilma's personal brand,

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:43.360
they say inside,

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:45.800
a duer visionary,

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.680
